3c11a4f5a1167f134cb24a2dac99e711260edf45516c630484fea9600"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164425" :question/id #uuid "e1e07339-84d1-526a-a86d-71372b557ab9" :question/math-academy-id "q-164425" :question/problem "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}=1}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(0,3)$ with semi-axes of lengths $5$ and $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164425/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36c5224a-eccc-5ea9-8719-2b0dc2ddb44d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186124808 :question/answer-fields 17592186121870] {:db/id "q-35569/selection/ma-v1/45a750002f0afc8232d16aec48e47a6c5830566c87f78a8c84915257684eac2d/79bc806bc76ca8329c04fede1fe6be3f2b747240d34315f2b1f1a1c2d7ba4e08" :answer/id #uuid "e78a8124-6354-59a5-b329-269bfa002c16" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse centered at $(-1,2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $2$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35569/selection/ma-v1/45a750002f0afc8232d16aec48e47a6c5830566c87f78a8c84915257684eac2d/3b69a7cfdd9430350e7001de785aef471ad65c07d437b87e705e6bd203ac6f42" :answer/id #uuid "359ba9ed-7b36-5bb2-a928-611685a4364d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$" :db/ensure 