30566c87f78a8c84915257684eac2d/71f4026ae7fbd7133cdce31517dd8f4d3c1753cb4aed6affb2ba2d1886c5ca86" "q-35569/selection/ma-v1/45a750002f0afc8232d16aec48e47a6c5830566c87f78a8c84915257684eac2d/d5cdeb8dff09edc863a519b95a6cc347403eee0a042abd863b01bcbf5e51f8cc" "q-35569/selection/ma-v1/45a750002f0afc8232d16aec48e47a6c5830566c87f78a8c84915257684eac2d/054462a85fa9226928c7598f47d646ab65bcfd74351b64558f03b04a305dbe39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35569"] :question/problem "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35569/selection/ma-v1/45a750002f0afc8232d16aec48e47a6c5830566c87f78a8c84915257684eac2d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-164417/selection/e32823cdeb320fbc7c020cfe5b9d2508ac7b5feb79182d9be5dd94e037be0949" :answer/id #uuid "72f918f9-d6a9-52a1-945f-93828c686818" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola centered at $(5,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164417/selection/5fa203c3fcea0916659b39d64a0565e556ceae774332a7e84808400b122c12a5" :answer/id #uuid "06a96e7c-b1b6-5224-8ad7-f72c5ce892d2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola centered at $(5,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164417/selection/809db055234655