nswer-field/choices ["q-164419/selection/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf" "q-164419/selection/d686d4590282c472541b22ffea5a17a81116c92013d11ca888890e717aedff0b" "q-164419/selection/2a3362e93098c994cf86eb2f63bc9e9a2d90fbccea33ee3c570287470f804f50" "q-164419/selection/504c164a71abe1ce9d3de13ad495cbaf6df7f406afe50b734fdf2697821e0b4b" "q-164419/selection/5b4a2143819b3bc91bb79c808bf38669d24eee5b72de66f225aff29beb4914d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164419" :question/id #uuid "8d66ef88-b3f7-5660-97bc-e01cb35d783f" :question/math-academy-id "q-164419" :question/problem "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(x-1)^{2}=3y?$" :question/worked-solution "The full expression describing all points on our parabolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}=3y,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:(x-1)^{2}=3y}.\n$$\n\nThis is an upward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(1,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-164419/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36c5224a-eccc-5ea9-8719-2b0dc2ddb44d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164419"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164415/selection/e5a95af398086ad96d04af715a4091221e92fcc2a77cc6f5dfb366708191f280" :answer/id #uuid "2e8674ab-e315-5efe-bf50-c302f17a7768" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{2}$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164415/selection/68bffd8007fc5b28cbce11341fc1d13a9bc2d32075bda5d488cd297ae7094437" :answer/id #uuid "170e12cf-bb71-5428-a64b-fbac5bb0e3f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164415/selection/e2a384ffd47965ea538d83060dbf10a43396d0fd5be9222fe5cc8bae5ad70ebe" :answer/id #uuid "d191ff0f-d416-506b-a474-c666f165354c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$10$ and $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164415/selection/104f49b666e7259fd60a1cd90040a9ce45c5d9b7c5e4055cd3626c1ad80a54bb" :answer/id #uuid "4dc6833a-3109-5cc5-955c-4b43c0b4fea8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164415/selection/d826542d60cf90edb1a08622a3232b5f60ac38a470abdd32b384ab4acb717119" :answer/id #uuid "da31ce0b-ba99-547e-b9e8-883287d38071" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164415/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "41d16978-9a2d-561d-933e-9c51c4124ec6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164415/selection/d826542d60cf90edb1a08622a3232b5f60ac38a470abdd32b384ab4acb717119" :answer-field/choices ["q-164415/selection/e5a95af398086ad96d04af715a4091221e92fcc2a77cc6f5dfb366708191f280" "q-164415/selection/68bffd8007fc5b28cbce11341fc1d13a9bc2d32075bda5d488cd297ae7094437" "q-164415/selection/e2a384ffd47965ea538d83060dbf10a43396d0fd5be9222fe5cc8bae5ad70ebe" "q-164415/selection/104f49b666e7259fd60a1cd90040a9ce45c5d9b7c5e4055cd3626c1ad80a54bb" "q-164415/selection/d826542d60cf90edb1a08622a3232b5f60ac38a470abdd32b384ab4acb717119"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164415" :question/id #uuid "6fceebe4-a56d-5581-86c4-4cef01c078e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-164415" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic cylinder $2(x+6)^{2}-5{y}^{2}=10$ and the plane $z=5$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=5,$ we substitute $z=5$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+6)^{2}-5{y}^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164415/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbeda26-2fc0-5195-be26-ae79c72fc7bf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164415"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35363"] :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the elliptic cylinder $9{x}^{2}+2(y-1)^{2}=18$ and the plane $z=1$ onto the $xy$-plane is an ellipse. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the ellipse?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=1,$ we substitute $z=1$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+2(y-1)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{(3)^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with semi-axes of lengths $\\sqrt{2}$ and $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-164398/selection/6f6b7bcb2effc34c4bfda214ea9a07561e05af0085ccad870393b9c98a1c0860" :answer/id #uuid "6826f8e0-8569-5f32-b740-21b9fdd97887" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The line $x=5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164398/selection/d05e21ee42532b00617a4c1ad1898f1f08c1e2f0a2261c3e6e959968df9eb1e7" :answer/id #uuid "3348313e-e93b-53fe-950a-778491fc9c92" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The line $x=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164398/selection/2af833fb5e1c5eb8193f8b2039f51a026cf9fd9fc24fd57df34c965ba139f735" :answer/id #uuid "723c343c-0f47-51d8-bb35-a3619d08f927" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The hyperbola $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164398/selection/9906d366499354691bbe89352dbb8e6d8c0f0dc2c49e657d464ca7becb01a902" :answer/id #uuid "82963d38-17d9-5f5d-a422-6a77747d67c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The lines $x=1$ and $x=5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164398/selection/be8a410c1a7f119e29c6a82759f4642029dd54d377c8de119de436e95816ec8f" :answer/id #uuid "89640ad3-319c-5b7c-9cbb-3d9cc87141f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164398/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "31747716-6593-5f8a-8b90-395a6a655b06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164398/selection/9906d366499354691bbe89352dbb8e6d8c0f0dc2c49e657d464ca7becb01a902" :answer-field/choices ["q-164398/selection/6f6b7bcb2effc34c4bfda214ea9a07561e05af0085ccad870393b9c98a1c0860" "q-164398/selection/d05e21ee42532b00617a4c1ad1898f1f08c1e2f0a2261c3e6e959968df9eb1e7" "q-164398/selection/2af833fb5e1c5eb8193f8b2039f51a026cf9fd9fc24fd57df34c965ba139f735" "q-164398/selection/9906d366499354691bbe89352dbb8e6d8c0f0dc2c49e657d464ca7becb01a902" "q-164398/selection/be8a410c1a7f119e29c6a82759f4642029dd54d377c8de119de436e95816ec8f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164398" :question/id #uuid "3402cf6a-d8e4-5082-a8db-072c1ad24c36" :question/math-academy-id "q-164398" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =3\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =1,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $x=1$ and $x=5$ in the $xy$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-164398/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbeda26-2fc0-5195-be26-ae79c72fc7bf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164398"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164400/selection/185b0fd903f079a2c84429a3c92c1df855eb3b0828f1a8335238d05d490e39df" :answer/id #uuid "d3c1db30-d60a-53f3-b2a2-cdbb3c4e4898" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The parabola $(x+3)^{2}=6z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164400/selection/e74f9ed7f7328611501e437050ec307578b8bf855df548dbe730911f435a2c07" :answer/id #uuid "ec1267fb-48d3-5536-8811-3e6dd8eb8aa7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The lines $y=-3$ and $y=15$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164400/selection/3e2cf808937f0a908407f8e7dea043e9af4e083ec6968da595a546b2280d7dcc" :answer/id #uuid "8a033994-7206-5d38-87a5-81db2249f53f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The parabola ${x}^{2}=6(z-3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164400/selection/2557e93940a17fe9dd763e57b674c0ee8cadf1f7aac7c717efc20462908c4050" :answer/id #uuid "b538c52f-58f4-525c-90b0-595d1bce9948" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The line $y=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164400/selection/4307290e4713999ac61deb15f67a5eaffb505a852815323e637790f075f89354" :answer/id #uuid "af9dd4a1-d1b8-5217-b51b-6f766f3b34c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The line $y=\\frac{3}{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164400/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "84a4f3de-bd74-5c02-a46d-c1fe74093a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164400/selection/4307290e4713999ac61deb15f67a5eaffb505a852815323e637790f075f89354" :answer-field/choices ["q-164400/selection/185b0fd903f079a2c84429a3c92c1df855eb3b0828f1a8335238d05d490e39df" "q-164400/selection/e74f9ed7f7328611501e437050ec307578b8bf855df548dbe730911f435a2c07" "q-164400/selection/3e2cf808937f0a908407f8e7dea043e9af4e083ec6968da595a546b2280d7dcc" "q-164400/selection/2557e93940a17fe9dd763e57b674c0ee8cadf1f7aac7c717efc20462908c4050" "q-164400/selection/4307290e4713999ac61deb15f67a5eaffb505a852815323e637790f075f89354"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164400" :question/id #uuid "7c06a8e8-6e3d-50f3-ae2e-200f38471a76" :question/math-academy-id "q-164400" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(x+3)^{2}=6y?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+3)^{2} & =6y \\\\ 9 & =6y \\\\ y & =\\frac{9}{6} \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a line in the $yz$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-164400/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbeda26-2fc0-5195-be26-ae79c72fc7bf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164400"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164411/selection/8b83ad520c122b6bf9f0447fd08ee7748fd4a02ebbad7be118c0cd4d30cc7890" :answer/id #uuid "ba0aeada-f80b-5eac-a5c3-44173949397a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164411/selection/ca19c26ffde1877c79d66bf7da309be5025c0ec8c718d95953d8c5cfa14dcc54" :answer/id #uuid "172fd8c6-f2e5-5640-88ed-61a271db7548" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164411/selection/5a05eb07a343e37ff67585adb95517191778ce43ec136b94ea103266bbe9f740" :answer/id #uuid "efd4100e-a77a-5b6d-8659-6d531d4fe79d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164411/selection/a1d3a0bfb4d700856d9fb14d1d861ba0bbc78f4b7d79ba9aec61a9bd1e355235" :answer/id #uuid "9771d26b-18a5-57ec-ab5c-803911edb87a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164411/selection/2241d0d98a22b3d525c08b2a741725081d8d666dd3966b75a025218a344e943e" :answer/id #uuid "581a880f-0bee-593e-a0fe-021b2f89e73b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164411/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b90d15e-01af-5ee6-9eb1-1df6cf3b7bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164411/selection/8b83ad520c122b6bf9f0447fd08ee7748fd4a02ebbad7be118c0cd4d30cc7890" :answer-field/choices ["q-164411/selection/8b83ad520c122b6bf9f0447fd08ee7748fd4a02ebbad7be118c0cd4d30cc7890" "q-164411/selection/ca19c26ffde1877c79d66bf7da309be5025c0ec8c718d95953d8c5cfa14dcc54" "q-164411/selection/5a05eb07a343e37ff67585adb95517191778ce43ec136b94ea103266bbe9f740" "q-164411/selection/a1d3a0bfb4d700856d9fb14d1d861ba0bbc78f4b7d79ba9aec61a9bd1e355235" "q-164411/selection/2241d0d98a22b3d525c08b2a741725081d8d666dd3966b75a025218a344e943e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164411" :question/id #uuid "25bdc329-60cf-56f4-84fa-3414d97450cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-164411" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic cylinder $3(x+1)^{2}-6(z-2)^{2}=12$ and the plane $y=1$ onto the $xz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $y=1,$ we substitute $y=1$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $y$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+1)^{2}-6(z-2)^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{(2)^{2}}-\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $2$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164411/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbeda26-2fc0-5195-be26-ae79c72fc7bf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164411"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8226"] :question/problem "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1?$" :question/worked-solution "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1, \\qquad z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k \\in \\mathbb{R}$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : \\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1\\right\\}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left\\{ (x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : \\dfrac{x^2}{3^2} + \\dfrac{(y+1)^2}{1^2} = 1\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(0,-1)$ with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8227"] :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac {x^2} 2 +  \\dfrac {(y-2)^2}4  = 1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =2\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =0,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=0$ and $y=4$ in the $yz$-plane." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
